-- title:
--   Degree bound over L(j(q^N)) at level N²M'
-- statement:
--   Fix integers $N,M'\ge 1$ and a field $L$ of characteristic zero. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ (Laurent series over $L$) and assume $K =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, $K$ is generated over $L$ inside $L((q))$ by the image of $F₀$ under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to L((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q}\to L$, where $F₀$ is the subfield [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ attached to the group $\Gamma =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH (N ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH N M')`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), namely the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ consisting of those $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(N^2M')$ whose lower-right entry reduces, modulo $N^2M'$, to a unit lying in the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/N^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$, i.e. congruent to $1$ modulo $N$. Assume further that $K$ contains an element $j$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the } j\text{-numerator power series})$, i.e. of the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-invariant, and an element $y$ whose Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L N`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), the substitution $q \mapsto q^N$ applied to that $j$-expansion over $L$. The conclusion is that $K$ is a finite extension of the intermediate field $L(y)$ generated by $y$ over $L$ inside $K$, and that $$[K : L(y)] \le [\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) : \Gamma \cdot \{\pm 1\}],$$ the index of the subgroup generated by $\Gamma$ together with $-1$.
--
--   This is the upper half of the degree count for the $q$-expansion function field of the modular curve of level $N^2M'$ with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $N$, measured over the rational line spanned by $j(q^N)$, the $j$-invariant of the level-$N$ Tate curve, rather than over $L(j(q))$. It feeds the density statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.dense_range_classify_of_jOf_eq_jqNModC_of_exists_ringHom_gamma0Pow_of_finiteType`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.dense_range_classify_of_jOf_eq_jqNModC_of_exists_ringHom_gamma0Pow_of_finiteType), where the finiteness of $K$ over $L(j(q^N))$ and the explicit index bound are both used.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_finiteDimensional_and_finrank_adjoin_le_index_of_coe_eq_jqNModC_of_eq_laurentBaseChange_levelH.lean

